  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOL: Moldova Energy Security Activity (MESA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the Moldova Energy Security Activity project implemented by the United States Agency for International Development, is to strengthen energy security in Moldova by: (1) advancing physical and market integration of the Moldovan energy sector with Europe; (2) increasing renewable energy integration; and also (3) increasing investment in energy efficiency and domestic power generation, particularly through increased adoption of renewable energy technologies. Long-term goals to diversify market sources will allow Moldova to select energy partners that help the country meet its clean energy goals, while also promoting energy security and improving climate resilience. The project will promote the adoption of green technologies in the energy sector and reduction fossil fuel consumption in Moldova, thus, will contribute significantly to the reduction of greenhouse gas emissions. Moldova Energy Security Activity project will make a critical environmental contribution to Moldova by laying the groundwork for future investment in renewable energy generation and energy efficiency in Moldova.</narrative>
  </description>
